<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan receives three bids for 6,000 T palm oil.</title>
<headline>Pakistan receives three bids for 6,000 T palm oil.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan received three bids on Thursday for 6,000 tonnes of RBD palm oil for shipment by December 31 and the lowest was $545.90 per tonne C&amp;F, dealers said.</p>
<p>The bids were opened by the state-run Trading Corporation of Pakistan (TCP), which buys vegetable oils for the state-run Ghee Corporation of Pakistan.</p>
<p>Results of the bids would be announced later in the day, one dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
